      "answer": "Asia Pacific forms the largest concentration, dominating the right side, while Western Europe is heavily clustered in the lower-left. The other regions occupy smaller, compact blocks: North America, Eastern Europe, and Australasia near the top; Latin America in a narrow middle band; and the Middle East and Africa running through the center toward the bottom.",
