    "graphrag": {
      "answer": "The chart contains 101 rectangular marks distributed across seven regions: Asia Pacific, Australasia, Eastern Europe, Latin America, Middle East and Africa, North America, and Western Europe. [G7] The distribution is concentrated most heavily in Asia Pacific with 35 marks and Western Europe with 29 marks. [G2] [G6] Together, Asia Pacific and Western Europe account for 64 of the 101 marks, or about 63.4% of the total. [G7] [G2] [G6] Middle East and Africa forms a secondary concentration with 13 marks, followed by North America with nine marks. [G4] [G8] The remaining regions have relatively small representations: Eastern Europe has seven marks, Latin America has six, and Australasia has two. [G5] [G3] [G1]",
